# =============================================================================
# Copy to `.env.local` for development. NEVER commit `.env.local`.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT — the identity shim
#
# Lets you run the app with no Cloudflare account by declaring who you are.
# BOTH variables are required: a stray email alone does nothing.
#
# This is an authentication bypass. It is guarded three ways (see
# src/auth/config.ts) and the app REFUSES TO BOOT if either variable is present
# while NODE_ENV=production. Do not try to work around that.
#
# Seeded development accounts (src/server/db.ts):
#   admin@ionic.in    ADMIN
#   manager@ionic.in  MANAGER
#   alice@ionic.in    EMPLOYEE, reports to manager
#   bob@ionic.in      EMPLOYEE, reports to manager
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CRM_ALLOW_DEV_IDENTITY=1
CRM_DEV_IDENTITY_EMAIL=alice@ionic.in

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRODUCTION — Cloudflare Access. Set these as Worker SECRETS, not here:
#   wrangler secret put CRM_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN
#   wrangler secret put CRM_ACCESS_AUD
#
# CRM_ACCESS_AUD is the AUD tag of THIS Access application, not a team-wide
# value. Without it the audience check is skipped and a token minted for any
# other application in the same Cloudflare team would be accepted — which is why
# the app refuses to start without it.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRM_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=yourteam.cloudflareaccess.com
# CRM_ACCESS_AUD=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRODUCTION — database (milestone M11, not yet wired)
# Supabase project pinned to ap-south-1 (Mumbai). Worker secret only.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRM_DATABASE_URL=
